            <div class="prose max-w-none" x-show="lang === 'en'" x-cloak>
                <h2>Background: The Real Cost of an Empty Balance</h2>
<p>When a utility app team was pushing toward their quarterly KPI, no one noticed their account balance hit zero after finance left for the day. Three key ad sets went offline for six hours. The aftermath revealed not just lost conversions during that window, but an additional two weeks of elevated costs as the algorithm relearned its audience targeting.</p>
<p>Balance alerts aren't optional—they're essential infrastructure for scaled campaigns. This SOP applies to teams managing Meta, Google, TikTok, and other major platforms.</p>
<hr />
<h2>Step 1: Set Up Multi-Tier Balance Alerts</h2>
<h3>Alert Trigger Conditions</h3>
<p>Configure three alert levels based on your daily spend patterns:</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Alert Level</th>
<th>Trigger Condition</th>
<th>Notification Method</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Low Risk</td>
<td>Balance &lt; 2x daily spend</td>
<td>Email digest</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Medium Risk</td>
<td>Balance &lt; 1x daily spend</td>
<td>Email + team chat</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>High Risk</td>
<td>Balance &lt; 0.5x daily spend</td>
<td>SMS + phone call + priority message</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<h3>Configuration Checklist</h3>
<ol>
<li><strong>Calculate daily spend</strong>: Use the 7-day rolling average of actual spend, not a fixed number</li>
<li><strong>Redundant channels</strong>: Configure at least two notification channels to avoid missed alerts</li>
<li><strong>Time-aware settings</strong>: High-risk alerts after hours should notify both on-call staff and supervisors</li>
</ol>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Tip</strong>: Meta Business Suite has notification settings, Google Ads has budget tools with alerts, and TikTok Ads supports balance reminders in Account Center.</p>
</blockquote>
<hr />
<h2>Step 2: Configure Auto-Recharge</h2>
<h3>When Auto-Recharge Works</h3>
<p>Auto-recharge suits situations where:<br />
- Daily spend is relatively stable<br />
- Finance can authorize pre-approved charges<br />
- You manage multiple accounts manually</p>
<h3>Setup Process</h3>
<ol>
<li><strong>Verify platform support</strong>: Google Ads and Amazon Ads support invoice payments and auto-recharge; Meta Business supports credit card charges; TikTok Ads has auto-recharge in select regions</li>
<li><strong>Set recharge amount and frequency</strong>: Configure "recharge X when balance drops below Y," where X covers 2-3 days of spend</li>
<li><strong>Confirm finance compliance</strong>: Align with finance on auto-debit limits and reconciliation processes</li>
</ol>
<h3>Important Notes</h3>
<ul>
<li>Auto-recharges may cluster on weekends or holidays—alert finance in advance</li>
<li>Platform processing delays mean auto-recharge shouldn't be your only safety net</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h2>Step 3: Define Manual Intervention Thresholds</h2>
<h3>When Human Action Is Required</h3>
<p>Operations staff should intervene manually in these scenarios:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>New account cold start</strong>: Spend fluctuates significantly, making auto-rules unreliable</li>
<li><strong>Campaign冲刺期 (Sprint periods)</strong>: Daily spend may be 3-5x normal levels; existing thresholds become obsolete</li>
<li><strong>After hours</strong>: When auto-recharge fails or platform issues occur</li>
</ul>
<h3>Daily Operations Checklist</h3>
<ul>
<li>[ ] Check all active account balances first thing each morning</li>
<li>[ ] Review today's budget plan and projected spend</li>
<li>[ ] Confirm any pending recharge orders</li>
<li>[ ] Verify with finance on any pending payments</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h2>Step 4: Emergency Response Protocols</h2>
<h3>Scenario 1: Recharge Delay</h3>
<ol>
<li>Submit an expedited recharge request via platform backend</li>
<li>Contact your account manager or agency to accelerate processing</li>
<li>Temporarily shift budget to a backup account if available</li>
<li>Log downtime duration for later performance attribution</li>
</ol>
<h3>Scenario 2: Payment Declined</h3>
<ol>
<li>Check common causes: credit limit, expiry date, bank fraud blocks</li>
<li>Switch to an alternative payment method (PayPal, bank transfer)</li>
<li>Coordinate with finance to update the payment account</li>
</ol>
<h3>Scenario 3: Platform System Outage</h3>
<ol>
<li>Confirm systemic issues via platform status pages or community forums</li>
<li>Screenshot account data and save support ticket records</li>
<li>After recovery, request credit or extended campaign duration from the platform</li>
</ol>
<hr />
<h2>Key Takeaway</h2>
<p>The core principle: <strong>Catch problems before they happen, not after.</strong></p>
<p>Operations teams should integrate this SOP into daily workflows, review alert effectiveness regularly, and adjust thresholds as business scale evolves. If you're managing multiple ad accounts, connect with 以渔数媒's operations team—we can help configure alert systems and recharge workflows.</p>
